<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "RecordingStudioUser",
    subtitle: "Profile editing and access-controlled users reporting for a Recording Studio host application.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render FlatPack::Card::Component.new(style: :default) do |card| %>
      <% card.header do %>
        <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
          title: "Profile workflow",
          subtitle: "Each signed-in user manages only their own global profile.",
          variant: :h3,
          class: "mb-0 pb-0"
        ) %>
      <% end %>

      <% card.body do %>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6">
          <li><code>My profile</code> opens the mounted profile at <code>/recording_studio_users/profile</code>.</li>
          <li>Profile edits are global to the signed-in user and do not depend on the selected workspace root.</li>
          <li>Devise sign-in and the Recording Studio root switcher remain host application behavior.</li>
          <li>Use <code>admin@admin.com</code> / <code>Password</code> or <code>member@admin.com</code> / <code>Password</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Card::Component.new(style: :outlined) do |card| %>
      <% card.header do %>
        <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
          title: "Users reporting",
          subtitle: "The users report is a site-level Admin-root workflow.",
          variant: :h3,
          class: "mb-0 pb-0"
        ) %>
      <% end %>

      <% card.body do %>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 list-decimal pl-5">
          <li>Open <code>Admin</code> at <code>/recording_studio_users/admin</code>.</li>
          <li>The seeded <code>admin@admin.com</code> has Admin-root access and can open the read-only users report.</li>
          <li>The seeded <code>member@admin.com</code> can edit a profile but cannot open the Admin-root report.</li>
          <li>Workspace roots and the Admin root are separate: selecting a workspace does not grant reporting access.</li>
        </ol>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Card::Component.new(style: :outlined) do |card| %>
      <% card.header do %>
        <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
          title: "Host responsibilities",
          subtitle: "RecordingStudioUser integrates with services the host owns.",
          variant: :h3,
          class: "mb-0 pb-0"
        ) %>
      <% end %>

      <% card.body do %>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
          The host provides <code>User</code>, Devise, the Admin root, RecordingStudioAccessible grants, and root-switcher configuration. RecordingStudioUser supplies mounted profile and reporting interfaces without changing those responsibilities.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <% card.footer do %>
        <a href="https://github.com/bowerbird-app/flatpack"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer"
           class="inline-flex">
          <%= render FlatPack::Button::Component.new(
            text: "View FlatPack documentation",
            style: :primary,
            size: :md
          ) %>
        </a>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render FlatPack::Card::Component.new(style: :default) do |card| %>
      <% card.header do %>
        <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
          title: "Documentation and diagnostics",
          subtitle: "Inspect the integration without changing product behavior.",
          variant: :h3,
          class: "mb-0 pb-0"
        ) %>
      <% end %>

      <% card.body do %>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6">
          <li>Install with <code>bin/rails generate recording_studio_user:install</code>.</li>
          <li>Read <code>Install</code>, <code>Config</code>, and <code>Routes and integrations</code> for host setup.</li>
          <li><code>Recordable types</code>, <code>Recordings tree</code>, and <code>Gem Views</code> are diagnostics.</li>
          <li>Diagnostics do not make profiles recording-backed, recordable-backed, or root-scoped.</li>
        </ul>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
